    <briefdescription>
<para>Managed scalar value: an <computeroutput><ref refid="class_m2_1_1_element_impl" kindref="compound">M2::ElementImpl</ref>&lt;<ref refid="unionring__elem" kindref="compound">ring_elem</ref>&gt;</computeroutput> that initialises itself through the parent <computeroutput><ref refid="class_coefficient_ring_r" kindref="compound">CoefficientRingR</ref></computeroutput>. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Holds the wrapped <computeroutput><ref refid="unionring__elem" kindref="compound">ring_elem</ref></computeroutput> so callers do not have to call <computeroutput><ref refid="class_coefficient_ring_r_af9205fc585fe72e91eea2a427d851843_1af9205fc585fe72e91eea2a427d851843" kindref="member">init</ref></computeroutput> / <computeroutput><ref refid="class_coefficient_ring_r_a63b417ef02718d6363198e7a83ea71e8_1a63b417ef02718d6363198e7a83ea71e8" kindref="member">clear</ref></computeroutput> by hand. Constructors initialise to zero or copy from an existing element via the ring. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
